WEBVTT

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.250
It's so cold.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.050
ls it morning already?

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.310
Oh, no wonder it didn't ring.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.100
Yunocchi, let's go to school.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.900
Miya? Why are you here?

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.950
My body feels so heavy.
l don't I think can move...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.330
Give up and come out.
You're completely surrounded!

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.420
Huh? Did the alarm clock ring?

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.850
Tell me, tell me, what color is in season now?

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.110
Smiling white

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.520
Tearful blue

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.190
Let's mix them together and find out

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:38.530
Today is sunny, so take out your canvas

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.240
Have some ice cream and lemon soda

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.910
Then draw some exciting and colorful toppings

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.960
Hey, rough sketch, please

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.880
Let's do a self portrait contest

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.630
Yuno

00:01:54.630 --> 00:02:01.100
All right! Don't get grouchy later

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.890
Miyako

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.100
Hiro

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:08.230
When the switch is flipped, I go wa-ha-ha

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.600
Sae

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:14.570
l hope everyone is having a great time

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.110
The race is on

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.900
I've gotta finish my apple quickly

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.490
No, that's not for eating

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:25.160
Let's take it easy

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:30.120
Fruits are our display models

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.960
So start drawing

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.800
It's our homework

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.680
Sniffle, sniffle...

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.730
Yunocchi, let's go to school.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.900
Yunocchi?

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.540
Give up and come out.
You're completely surrounded!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.790
Hey, what are you doing?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.500
February 13th

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.500
Heart and Body

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.630
Sorry about that. Good morning.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.720
Wow, Yunocchi, you're all red!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.010
Are you all right? You must have a fever.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.470
I'm all right.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.270
Do you have a thermometer?

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.890
Yes, I do.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.030
38.2 degrees?
You'd better skip school and stay in bed.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.990
No, way. My body must be acting up.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.660
It's really cold today, isn't it?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.420
I'll get ready right away.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.880
Oh no!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.500
Yuno is acting strange.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.720
Get plenty of rest today.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.340
Sorry about this.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.850
Call my cell if you need me.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.680
If you don't feel better,
you'd better go to the hospital.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.390
Okay.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.310
Where's the closest hospital from here?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.690
The school nurse's office?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.030
Yunocchi, we're off.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.820
Take care.
Keep warm.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.750
I'm late for class.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.760
It's so cold.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.190
Brutus?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.190
Yunocchi, you're so late.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.860
It's going to be a busy day today.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.980
I'm sorry. I didn't hear the alarm.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.990
Here, this is yours. You have to make it whiter.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.870
Okay, but why Brutus?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.250
Because it's the basics of drawing.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.370
So cold...

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.880
It's because you aren't dressed warmly.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.970
Oh no, my face is hot. This is so embarrassing.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.180
Yuno, are you all right?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.350
Yes, I'm totally fine.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:45.110
Ms. Yoshinoya isn't around,
so I think she'll be absent today.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.530
She disappears when we're busy.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:56.080
She might be hiding somewhere at school,
so if you find her, let me know.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.670
And there was someone who
came to school late.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.210
It's the person who's wearing the short-sleeve
uniform in this cold weather.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.260
Don't get sick. That will be all.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:14.430
Whoa, the principal is upset,
but how did he know about me?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.190
Oh no, it's still hot.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.650
Just a dream...

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.530
I'm thirsty.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.210
I've gotta get back to the classroom,
or the principal will find me.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.790
Oh, that's right, the flour.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.720
What if Ms. Yoshinoya pops out?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.040
There's no way I can wear that.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.450
Fragile

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.450
Fresh Paint

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.450
Fire Awareness

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.670
Am I doing this right?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.550
l wonder where everyone has gone?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.090
I'm thirsty.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:35.050
Where did Ms. Yoshinoya go?

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.970
Has the next class already started?

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.900
Oh, the thermostat is acting up after all.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.290
Yunocchi!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.260
She's sleeping like a baby.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:17.970
She's still burning up.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.520
She's sweating a lot.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.310
It might be a bit cold, but put up with it.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.030
There's a mole.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.830
Okay, the other hand.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.920
Almost done...

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.050
There, finished.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:08.310
Oh, apple, I'm sorry.
l can't take it. I didn't know...

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.570
Huh? I was in the fifth grade
when I came here.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.070
Sir, what are you doing there?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.040
Thermostat...

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.620
Oh, that's right... I was going to fix it.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:14.210
My face isn't hot. Maybe I have been repaired.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.510
I'm back to normal.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:35.730
Yamabuki Jizo? So, I'm back.
l should have visited Dad and Mom.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.030
Berry Mart

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.400
<i>Green Tea</i>

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:42.320
Oh no, I don't have my wallet.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.920
Oh, a 100-yen sale is going on.
l must tell everyone about it.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.140
Where did I put my wallet?

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.180
Not here.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:15.770
ls that Chika? Why is she here?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:22.990
l shouldn't have seen her,
because I'm terrible at lying.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.410
No, I don't have my cellphone either.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.970
No way. It's really from Chika.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:45.430
Tomorrow is Valentine's Day.
Who's your valentine?

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:52.980
l don't have anyone.
Sorry to disappoint you. Message sent.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.480
Sending Mail

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.150
She already replied?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.110
Oh, it's Sae.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:03.740
How do you feel? I'll be back as soon as l
get some medicine at the nurse's office.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.240
I'd like a tablet type that's not so bitter.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.120
Send.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.180
ls it supposed to be an apple
shaped into a rabbit?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.480
l feel like I've had so many
different types of dreams.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.860
It's a little less hot.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.950
It's already this late. All classes are over.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.830
l feel like I'm forgetting something.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.330
Oh well...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.040
That must have been done by Miya.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.420
Excuse me!

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.170
Miyako, don't talk so loudly.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.090
It's okay.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:07.220
But isn't there someone resting?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.600
Why?

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.190
Why is she here?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.770
Good morning.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.030
Did you fake being sick?

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:25.070
How mean! I am sick.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.570
Then, why did you come to school?

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:32.040
Adults have adult's circumstances.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.330
What do you mean?

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:39.170
My parents forced me to go, saying
my cold wasn't serious enough.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.380
She acts like a bratty teen.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.420
<i>Incoming Mail</i>

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.420
Mail Received
1 Mail
Yuno

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.970
I'd like to have some cold medicine.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.970
Do you have any of the tablet type
that's not too bitter tasting?

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.560
Oh, you don't like the powdered type?

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.100
No, it's not for me.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.690
I've learned something new about you.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.990
The outside noise brings back
my childhood memories.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:15.660
l remember the outside sounded like that when
l couldn't go to school and stayed in bed.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.460
l wonder how Mom is doing?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.800
l wonder how Yuno is doing?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.090
l think she's okay.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.100
l hope she stayed in bed.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.100
Yunocchi!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.730
Oh, I fell asleep again.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.690
Coming...

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.810
We're back. How do you feel?

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.780
Welcome back. I feel a lot better.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.450
The nurse's office didn't have any tablets,
so we bought the syrup type they give kids.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.200
Oh, thank you.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:57.660
And apple juice. These boxes are small,
so it looked easier to drink.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.170
Egg Bolo
With Calcium

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.040
We also got some bite-size ''Egg Bolo'' cookies.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.330
Eh?

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.960
And this one to get some sugar.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.880
Kid's stuff.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:12.760
Has your fever gone down?
Your face doesn't look normal.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.520
Thank you so much.
I'm making you guys worry.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:21.520
Yeah, we were so worried.
You looked so red this morning.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:24.190
Yeah, you were acting up, Yunocchi.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.440
You haven't eaten, have you?
I'll fix some rice-porridge.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:30.950
You have to take your medicine too.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:35.030
Oh, but you've already done so much.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.790
Oh, c'mon.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.830
Here you go. Your porridge is ready.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.790
That looks tasty. Thank you very much.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.000
It's good.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.590
l like porridge.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:55.180
Come to think, all the students around
Yunocchi's desk were absent today.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.680
Really?

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.930
Yeah, Nakagawa and Kumada too.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:06.940
Miya, that's not around me,
but around you, right?

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.360
ls that right?

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.610
Some say morons...

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:11.240
...come in handy?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.160
How was Ms. Yoshinoya doing?

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.700
How did you know about her absence?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.450
Was she absent?

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:18.910
Yes, actually...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.580
Technically, she wasn't absent because
we found her in a certain location.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.130
A certain location?

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:29.550
It's hard to believe, but when we went to the
nurse's office to get your medicine...

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.300
The nurse...

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.840
...opened the curtain, and...

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.890
...Ms. Yoshinoya was sound asleep on the bed.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.510
Wha? I was looking for
Ms. Yoshinoya all day today.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:40.720
Say what?

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.730
l mean in my dreams,
l was outside all day today.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:53.110
l went to school, a factory to fix the thermostat,
Berry Mart, the cake shop and even the park.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.570
For what?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:59.120
Well, I went to school late,
and the principal was mad.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.160
A prophetic dream!

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.120
Really?

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.540
Really, really!

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:10.630
''Hi, class. Ms. Yoshinoya is absent today.
So, I'm here to fill in.''

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:13.170
Wow, you're pretty good.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:18.350
''Many students are sick, so be careful.''

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.560
''When you get home,
wash your hands and gargle.''

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.350
''When you go out, dress warmly.''

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.190
Amazing...

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:33.190
''Even if you think wet hair on a
cold day sounds cool,''

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:39.120
''if you go out like that and catch a cold,
l won't accept any excuses.''

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.870
Wow!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.370
So, Ms. Yoshinoya...

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.500
...got sick for that reason?!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.620
Thanks.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.960
Miya, you remembered all that?

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.000
I just tried, and it came out of my mouth.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.220
Thanks for the food.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.720
Oh no, you don't have to worry about me.
Go ahead and finish it.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.010
Yes, you can have it, Miya.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.390
But you should get another spoon,
or you'll catch a cold too.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:06.890
l don't think she will.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.520
Eh?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:15.240
Today I tried so hard to take
notes for Yunocchi, but...

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.530
But what?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.150
But you know...

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:24.450
You woke up and realized that
you fell asleep on doodles.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:25.450
Did you see me?

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:30.250
Miya, don't push yourself too hard,
like you did on this.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:35.090
What is that? It must have come
from an alternate dimension.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:39.220
l was going to ask you.
ls this supposed to look like a dog?

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:44.430
Maybe a fairy crafted it.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:48.060
I'm full now, so I'll have it tomorrow.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.900
Oh Yuno, what is it?

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:53.980
A rabbit.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.860
So, tomorrow is Valentine's Day.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.410
Hello guys, I'm an eater.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:03.990
I'm a cook.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.410
What about Sae?

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.330
She's a taker.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.710
Could that be because of your
dignified demeanor

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.540
that's sometimes more manly than men?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.710
What about you, Yuno?

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:23.260
l don't have anyone to give chocolate to.
Should I give one to the principal?

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:28.020
We're talking about which stereotype you fit,
like taker, giver or eater.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:33.060
l don't know. I don't remember much
about doing that kind of stuff.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.440
l tend to catch a cold and skip
classes this time of the year.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.610
That sounds totally Yunocchi.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.400
You think so?

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.620
Are you sleepy?

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:44.910
No!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.660
Maybe we should go.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.290
Bye, Yunocchi. I hope you feel better tomorrow.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.000
Get enough rest, okay?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.710
Goodnight.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.500
Thanks.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.310
Good!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.830
Sae?!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.490
Notebooks.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.500
Don't wake her up.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:37.880
l baked some cake, so she
can have it tomorrow.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.840
l brought my notes from last year.
Miyako isn't quite dependable.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.720
You are so kind, Sae.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:50.470
When I got sick last year,
you stayed by me all night long.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.520
l did?

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:57.110
l was so glad that you stayed
awake and sat next to me.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.190
Even the part about me waking up
to find myself getting crushed by you

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.190
is a happy memory.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.540
She's so cute, just like a real sister.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.790
You're the same, right?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.290
Yuno? Yeah, I like her.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.620
No, I mean you are...

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.210
That, I won't tell.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.050
Miya...

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.680
I'm thirsty and hungry.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.100
Whoa, a cake!

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:38.770
Sae must have brought these.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:52.080
So tasty, I couldn't be happier.
This is incredible.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.580
I'm so awake.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.130
End of February 13th

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.640
To Be Continued

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:21.360
It eventually fades into the tall sky

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.980
The voices

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.780
Bubble up and fade away

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:31.200
Fade away

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.910
They return to where they belong

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:44.420
And fuse together as they sparkle and collide

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:49.880
This body feels like one entity

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:53.050
Yet, it's made of infinity

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:56.470
Caught a falling drop of water

00:22:56.470 --> 00:23:02.480
And now I'm taking a closer look

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.110
Awakening Drive

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:09.530
Dash into the sky in our bare feet

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:13.740
Close your eyes, can you see it?

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.910
It's a rainbow bridge, let's run toward it

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.620
Awakening Drive

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:22.960
A dazzling spark will break a star into pieces

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:31.180
Scattering across the sky and falling,
now in my hands

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:37.810
l have a piece of a dream, shining so bright

00:23:37.810 --> 00:24:07.430
Next Episode

00:23:39.820 --> 00:23:41.580
Summer reminds me of cooking nabe stew.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:43.490
Dancing shirataki noodles, tofu, green onions...

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:46.080
Don't forget crab, shrimp,
daikon and chili pepper.

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:48.750
Why are you talking about
nabe stew in this heat?

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.880
Kimchi, boiled beef, Sumo-wrestler's stew...

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:53.210
I see happiness beyond the rising steam!

00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:55.420
Are you talking about some kind of trial game?

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:58.930
Only those who have passed
the ordeal will find out.

00:23:59.090 --> 00:24:02.930
Next Episode is
''July 14th: Cool and Comfy''

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:07.430
We'll be waiting at the Hidamari Apartments,
so please, join us again.
